 ## RCC Environment Artifact execution
 
+Keep the bundled RCC download/build pin separate from adapter compatibility.
+A version string is identification, not source, byte or functional qualification.
+For an operator-approved isolated override, retain the exact RCC source, producer
+receipt, platform, executable digest and required contract features; an unknown
+or unqualified tuple stays incompatible rather than entering a broad version range.
+Measure the selected executable again before use and keep its actual version and
+compatibility identity in fresh descriptors and process-local cache keys. The
+Environment Artifact digest alone does not bind the RCC executable that acquired
+or executes it. Changing binaries must invalidate preparation reuse and reject
+a stale execution descriptor until it is explicitly requalified. Preserve older
+receipts under their original source/binary tuple; a later source with the same
+version label or matching tree does not relabel an earlier executed binary.
+
 Managed spec-v2 Action packages use the provisional RCC runtime adapter only
 when `ACTIONS_RUNTIME_RCC_PROVIDER` or `ACTIONS_REAL_RCC_ARTIFACT_TEST`
 explicitly opts into artifact mode. Without either opt-in, legacy bootstrap
